# Client-side routing: every unmatched path is rewritten to index.html so
# /blog, /blog/:slug and /studio/* survive a hard refresh and a shared link.
# A 200 here is a rewrite, not a redirect — the URL in the address bar is left
# alone, which is what React Router needs to read it.
#
# The lead form POSTs to "/". Netlify runs form handling ahead of redirect
# rules, so this catch-all does not swallow it; if a submission ever does come
# back as HTML instead of the success page, point the form at /__forms.html
# instead and add a matching rule above this line.
/*    /index.html   200
